+# Monarch’s Journey targeted runtime trace plan
+
+## What can be observed
+
+It is not practical or useful to log every CPU instruction in CK2. It is practical to log the small set of functions that decide whether feat progress is active, evaluate the feat script, and recalculate score.
+
+A debugger breakpoint is temporary and in-memory; it does not permanently alter the executable or save files. A logging breakpoint can let CK2 continue normally after recording a hit.
+
+## Windows 3.3.3 V6/V7 targets
+
+Use the exact image-base virtual addresses below when debugging the May 2020 Windows executable:
+
+```text
+IsActiveForPlaythrough entry:       0x1407b8370
+CalcShouldTrack entry:              0x1407b8450
+CalcShouldTrack after active call:  0x1407b8469   ; AL is the active-check result
+UpdateFeatProgress entry:           0x1407b8e60
+Update after CalcShouldTrack:       0x1407b8e86   ; AL is the should-track result
+RecalcScore entry:                  0x1407b9340
+```
+
+The two duplicated outer caller gates tested by V7 are:
+
+```text
+0x140667146
+0x1407862e8
+```
+
+## What each result means
+
+| Observation | Interpretation |
+|---|---|
+| No hit at `UpdateFeatProgress` | An outer caller still skips the update routine, or the relevant game tick/caller is not running. |
+| `AL=0` at `0x1407b8469` | The loaded game is not considered active for the current Featured Ruler playthrough. This is the strongest current hypothesis. |
+| Active check passes, but `AL=0` at `0x1407b8e86` | A later time, game-state, Steam/achievement, or account-related predicate still rejects live tracking. |
+| Update is entered but no `RecalcScore` hit | The feat database/list or evaluation path is not initialized/populated after load. |
+| RecalcScore is hit but values do not change | The evaluator runs, but the current character/scope or feat script conditions do not produce a higher value. |
+| All functions hit and score changes | The issue was an update scheduling gate; then test save/reload persistence. |
+
+A full call stack at each hit is also useful. Symbols are not available in the Windows executable, so addresses are expected; the Linux symbols provide the labels above.
+
+## Recommended collection format
+
+A small text log is enough. For each hit, record:
+
+```text
+time since launch
+current game date if visible
+function label and VA
+AL/EAX at return checkpoints
+call stack addresses
+```
+
+No full process dump, account cache, credentials, or broad CK2 log archive is needed.
+
+## How data reaches the repository
+
+The sandbox cannot attach to the user’s Windows process directly. The user would run the prepared debugger/tracer on Windows, stop it after reproducing one failed update, and copy the small text log into the repository or attach it. A periodic upload is possible, but one controlled trace around a loaded save is preferable to continuous high-volume logging.
+
+## Safety
+
+- Keep the Internet disconnected.
+- Trace the verified V6 or V7 executable only.
+- Do not use `wipe_feats`.
+- Do not overwrite the two evidence saves.
+- Do not upload credentials, `pdx_login.txt`, account caches, or tokens.
