+# Windows CK2 3.3.3 V7 feat-update findings
+
+Date: 2026-08-21
+
+## Runtime fact that motivated this analysis
+
+The user reports that V6 loads the Featured Ruler save correctly, keeps the Monarch’s Journey interface, and restores the saved value `1`. New qualifying actions nevertheless do not increase feat progress or challenge score.
+
+This separates the remaining issue from V6 save selection/deserialization.
+
+## Static findings
+
+The verified stock Windows May 2020 3.3.3 executable was reconstructed from the repository’s Base64 parts and verified against:
+
+```text
+SHA-256: 656f4f482ed698958e1108938f7e5baff5b5dd31b3b310a7ea51386faca635d8
+```
+
+The V6 byte sequence was reproduced independently as:
+
+```text
+SHA-256: f5b7dfd6e23b63f6353bb74f89493af0bd3db909e2d09961a543c773668530b0
+```
+
+The shared in-game feat-update routine begins at:
+
+```text
+VA:       0x1407b8e60
+Raw:      0x007b8260
+```
+
+It is called from two duplicated Windows 3.3.3 callers:
+
+```text
+Caller 1: VA 0x140667150, raw call-site region 0x00666550
+Caller 2: VA 0x1407862f2, raw call-site region 0x007856f2
+```
+
+Immediately before the call, both callers perform the same logic:
+
+```asm
+cmp  byte ptr [global_flag], 0
+jne  accepted_update_path
+call readiness_or_trigger_predicate
+ test al, al
+je   skip_update
+accepted_update_path:
+call prepare_update_state
+call shared_feat_update
+```
+
+The two `je skip_update` branches are:
+
+| Raw offset | VA | V6 bytes | V7 bytes |
+|---:|---:|---|---|
+| `0x00666546` | `0x140667146` | `74 0d` | `90 90` |
+| `0x007856e8` | `0x1407862e8` | `74 0d` | `90 90` |
+
+V7 lets execution fall through to the existing normal update path. The shared routine still retains its own internal checks, including the existing V4/V5/V6 in-game tracking edit at raw `0x007b78eb`.
+
+## V7 candidate identity
+
+Applying only those two additional two-byte edits to exact V6 produces:
+
+```text
+Size:    24,753,368 bytes
+SHA-256: 0074af707665bb152d3592d8ba9320ea81e79e6f58edc218e22aa069b353aeb8
+```
+
+No save files or complete modified executable are stored in the repository. The V7 deliverables are guarded scripts that accept only exact V6 or exact V7 hashes.
+
+## Current interpretation
+
+The loaded campaign restores the serialized feat value but does not enter the normal live-evaluation path. V7 tests two duplicated outer caller gates narrowly.
+
+Cross-version matching against Linux now identifies an earlier and potentially stronger suspect: Windows `0x1407b8370` matches `CRulerFeatTracker::IsActiveForPlaythrough()`, which is called inside `CalcShouldTrackFeatProgress()` at `0x1407b8450`. V6/V7 do not bypass that earlier active-playthrough result. A runtime trace should record that return value before another permanent patch is considered.
+
+This is not proven until runtime tracing or a controlled V7 test shows whether a qualifying action increases progress. If the active check returns false after load, the next candidate should target only that offline Featured Ruler state gate. If the active check passes but progress still does not change, inspect the remaining time/achievement gate or feat-definition registration path.
